// Title: Flow log counts by target type, enabled state and identity; and by subscription and region
// Purpose: Coverage summary. Is every region covered, are flow logs enabled, do they carry an identity.
// Source table(s): Azure Resource Graph, resources (microsoft.network/networkwatchers/flowlogs)
// Parameters to edit: none.
// Notes/traps: an empty result means no flow logs at all in the visible subscriptions, treat that as a
//          finding, not as a clean run. VNet flow logs need a managed identity for storage access
//          when the storage account is locked down, a migrated flow log without identity shows
//          identity = NONE here.
resources
| where type =~ 'microsoft.network/networkwatchers/flowlogs'
| summarize flowLogs = count()
    by targetType = tostring(split(tostring(properties.targetResourceId), '/')[-2]),
       enabled = tostring(properties.enabled),
       identity = iff(isnull(identity), 'NONE', tostring(identity.type)),
       subscriptionId, region = location
| order by subscriptionId asc, region asc
